## Original Content
The US threatened Iran with what it called "the greatest financial offensive ever marshalled" as it prepared to ​roll out economic sanctions on Monday that target Iran's trade partners.

## Summary
The United States is threatening Iran with massive economic sanctions, described as 'the greatest financial offensive ever marshalled,' targeting Iran's trade partners. In response, Iran has threatened to halt oil exports from the Gulf region, escalating geopolitical tensions. This conflict highlights deepening disputes over energy security and international relations.

## Key Points
- The US vows to impose unprecedented economic sanctions on Iran.
- These sanctions are planned to roll out on Monday and will target Iran's trade partners.
- Iran threatens to stop Gulf oil exports in retaliation.
- This escalation could disrupt global oil supply and markets.


